# Copy to .env for local development: `cp .env.example .env`. Never commit the
# real .env (see .gitignore). Node 24's `--env-file-if-exists=.env` reads this
# automatically in the scripts that need it (start:dev, start, db:migrate,
# conformance, test) — no export, no dotenv package. A missing .env is not an
# error (the "-if-exists" form); the values below are only ever a default a
# real .env or a real `export` overrides.
#
# These values are for a machine with NO Docker and a native PostgreSQL 17 on
# the default port 5432 — this project's actual local development machine, not
# a placeholder. `docker-compose.yml` and CI (.github/workflows/conformance.yml)
# both use port 5433 instead, deliberately, so a developer's own native
# Postgres on the default 5432 is never confused with the disposable compose
# one — see decisions/2026-08.md, "docker-compose Postgres on port 5433, not
# 5432". `platform/config.ts`'s own hard-coded fallback (used only if neither
# this file nor a real export sets the variable) stays 5433 to match that
# compose/CI default; it is not changed by this file.

# The app/runtime connection — nexora_app (NOSUPERUSER, NOBYPASSRLS, never a
# table owner). Used by platform/config.ts's loadDbConfig() and, by default,
# by the conformance harness's live-DB tests (loadConformanceTestDbConfig()).
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://nexora_app:nexora_app_dev_only@localhost:5432/nexora

# The audit-write connection (platform/db/connections.ts's AUDIT_DB).
# Commented out, unlike DATABASE_URL above: defaults to DATABASE_URL when
# unset, so behavior today is byte-identical whether or not this line is
# here. Set this to a genuinely separate database only once that
# independence is actually needed — today AUDIT_DB and APP_DB point at the
# same PostgreSQL instance, so one outage takes both down together (see
# platform/db/connections.ts's own doc comment and RISK_REGISTER.md R-010).
# AUDIT_DATABASE_URL=

# The migration/schema-owner connection — nexora_migrate. Only the migration
# runner (platform/db/migrate-cli.ts) and the harness's schema-structure
# checks use this; it is never the role the running app or its tests query
# through, because it owns the tables it creates and would bypass RLS.
MIGRATE_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://nexora_migrate:nexora_migrate_dev_only@localhost:5432/nexora

# Optional override: point the conformance harness's live-DB self-tests at a
# different server/role than DATABASE_URL. Rarely needed — defaults to
# DATABASE_URL (the nexora_app role) if unset.
# CONFORMANCE_TEST_DATABASE_URL=

# Matches docker-compose.yml's redis service (host port 6380). Commented
# out, unlike DATABASE_URL/MIGRATE_DATABASE_URL above: nothing in this
# codebase reads this yet (no client dependency, no BullMQ) — the service
# exists so the compose/CI plumbing is proven before Phase 2's first queue
# consumer needs it. See PHASE_1_DEBT_CLOSURE.md D-2 and DECISION_LOG.md
# 2026-08-29.
# REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6380
